<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Research Report: Political News Exposure & Implicit Bias</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
        h1 { color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 10px; }
        h2 { color: #34495e; margin-top: 30px; }
        .section { margin-bottom: 40px; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0; }
        th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; text-align: left; }
        th { background-color: #f2f2f2; }
        .plot { max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 20px 0; }
        .alert { padding: 10px; background-color: #f8d7da; color: #721c24; border-radius: 4px; margin: 10px 0; }
        .success { background-color: #d4edda; color: #155724; }
        footer { margin-top: 50px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #eee; font-size: 0.9em; color: #666; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Impact of Self-Reported Political News Exposure on Implicit Political Bias</h1>
    <p><strong>Generated:</strong> {{ timestamp }}</p>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>1. Methods</h2>
        <p>This analysis examines the relationship between self-reported political news exposure frequency and implicit political bias (measured by the IAT D-score), testing for an interaction with political ideology.</p>
        <p><strong>Data Source:</strong> Project Implicit Political IAT Dataset</p>
        <p><strong>Primary Model:</strong> Linear Regression with interaction term: IAT_D ~ news_exposure_z * political_ideology</p>
        <p><strong>Robustness Checks:</strong> Bootstrap resampling (n=1000), Alpha sensitivity analysis, Covariate adjustment (age, gender, education), Binary ideology model.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>2. Primary Model Results</h2>
        {% if primary_model %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Term</th>
                    <th>Coefficient</th>
                    <th>Std Error</th>
                    <th>t-value</th>
                    <th>P-value</th>
                    <th>Significant?</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in primary_model.to_dict('records') %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row.get('term', 'N/A') }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row.get('coef', 0)) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row.get('std_err', 0)) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row.get('tvalue', 0)) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row.get('pvalue', 0)) }}</td>
                    <td>{% if row.get('pvalue', 1) < 0.05 %}Yes{% else %}No{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">No primary model results found.</div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>3. Interaction Plot</h2>
        {% if plots.interaction %}
        <img src="{{ plots.interaction }}" alt="Interaction Plot" class="plot">
        <p><em>Figure 1: Interaction between news exposure and political ideology on implicit bias.</em></p>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">Interaction plot not generated.</div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>4. Robustness Checks</h2>
        
        <h3>4.1 Bootstrap Distribution (n=1000)</h3>
        {% if plots.bootstrap %}
        <img src="{{ plots.bootstrap }}" alt="Bootstrap Distribution" class="plot">
        <p><em>Figure 2: Bootstrap distribution of the interaction coefficient.</em></p>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">Bootstrap plot not generated.</div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if bootstrap %}
        <p><strong>Bootstrap Summary:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Mean Coefficient: {{ "%.4f"|format(bootstrap['interaction_coef'].mean()) }}</li>
            <li>95% CI: [{{ "%.4f"|format(bootstrap['interaction_coef'].quantile(0.025)) }}, {{ "%.4f"|format(bootstrap['interaction_coef'].quantile(0.975)) }}]</li>
        </ul>
        {% endif %}

        <h3>4.2 Alpha Sensitivity</h3>
        {% if alpha_sweep %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Alpha Level</th>
                    <th>Significant?</th>
                    <th>Coefficient</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in alpha_sweep.to_dict('records') %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row.get('alpha_level', 'N/A') }}</td>
                    <td>{% if row.get('significant', False) %}Yes{% else %}No{% endif %}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row.get('coef', 0)) }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">Alpha sweep results not found.</div>
        {% endif %}

        <h3>4.3 Covariate Adjustment</h3>
        {% if covariate %}
        <p><strong>Covariate Model (adjusted for age, gender, education):</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Interaction Coefficient: {{ "%.4f"|format(covariate.iloc[0]['coef']) if not covariate.empty else 'N/A' }}</li>
            <li>P-value: {{ "%.4f"|format(covariate.iloc[0]['pvalue']) if not covariate.empty else 'N/A' }}</li>
        </ul>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">Covariate model results not found.</div>
        {% endif %}

        <h3>4.4 Binary Ideology Model</h3>
        {% if binary %}
        <p><strong>Binary Ideology Model (Left vs Right):</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Interaction Coefficient: {{ "%.4f"|format(binary.iloc[0]['coef']) if not binary.empty else 'N/A' }}</li>
            <li>P-value: {{ "%.4f"|format(binary.iloc[0]['pvalue']) if not binary.empty else 'N/A' }}</li>
        </ul>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">Binary model results not found.</div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>5. Power Analysis</h2>
        {% if power %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Metric</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in power.to_dict('records') %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row.get('metric', 'N/A') }}</td>
                    <td>{{ row.get('value', 'N/A') }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <div class="alert">Power analysis results not found.</div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>Report generated by the llmXive Automated Science Pipeline.</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>